      "id": 1,
      "text": "Bottineau was founded in 1883 as Oak Creek, a customs station and overnight stagecoach stop.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bottineau%2C_North_Dakota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town moved south in 1887 to align with the Great Northern Railway tracks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bottineau%2C_North_Dakota",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Bottineau’s name honors Pierre Bottineau, a Métis pioneer and land speculator from 1814–1895.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bottineau%2C_North_Dakota",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The world’s largest turtle, Tommy Turtle, is a landmark at Bottineau Winter Park.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
